PURPOSE of /kernel/power-management/rapl/powercap_multirun
Description: Simple test of powercap.
Author: Erik Hamera <ehamera@redhat.com>

RAPL = Running Average Power Limit

Check RAPL functions. It measures power consumption on idle and on full load on all cores.
Then it will cap it to the average power and measures power consumption under full load again.

There are two magic constants in it:
- measure time is 30 seconds
- 10% maximal difference between measured and capped value until test is going to fail

These constants are __NOT__ emerging from intel's datasheets or something like that. They
__ARE__ just wild guess which should suppress false alarms due to started daemons and other
fluctuations. Feel free to change it if your guess is better, than mine.

The powercap test fails on some computers the first time and works properly after that.
This test is the exact copy of the powercap test, but the testing phase is tripled with
sleep between 2nd and 3rd test.

It works on RHEL 6.7.

